        "name": "Juno 0.1.10",
        "notes": "# Juno runs again on a newer browser, with a calmer notch and safer teams\n\n## What's new\n\n- A newer browser (Chromium 156). Chrome 157 became the stable version, and Juno refuses a browser two versions behind for your safety, so 0.1.9 and earlier would not start. This build brings it back, with dozens of security fixes.\n- A calmer notch: while Juno fills a form or works through a page it shows one steady line per step (\"Filling Email\", \"Filling Phone\") instead of flickering between \"Looking at the open tabs\" and \"Reading the page\".\n- A chat and its tabs read as one: in the sidebar they sit on one card with a thread to each tab, lit when any of them is in front, and fold to one row.\n- Pinned chats in your own order: drag them, use Option+Command+Up/Down, or Move up and Move down in the menu.\n- Delete your account from Settings > Account (it asks you to sign in again first; a team you own with others must be passed on before).\n\n## Teams\n\n- A teammate's request only reads the team it was asked in, and never what you shared privately with someone else.\n- Files: your yes card shows each file and the start of a text file; files that hold a password or key are never attached; programs are refused; an \"Always\" rule never lets a file through without asking.\n- Names can no longer carry hidden characters that fake a line on your lock screen or a yes card.\n- Leaving a team stops the asks you made there; admins cannot make other admins or remove them.\n\n## Privacy and safety\n\n- What you type in the address bar is no longer kept in a file, and words addressed to Juno never go to a search engine's suggestions.\n- Open tabs are saved encrypted only.\n- Clearing your history also clears the sidebar's archive of closed tabs.\n- Hidden text on a page is marked as not visible, so the agent does not take it as what the page shows.\n- Downloads that pretend to be a document but are an app are blocked even when padded with look-alike spaces.\n\n## Fixes\n\n- In the sidebar, the page shown beside a chat is no longer closed by the tab clean-up when you click another tab.\n- Pressing Enter twice quickly in a menu no longer drops the second key.\n- The browser no longer quits when a chat leaves a split view while you are on another tab.",
